rrant there is at  least in theory barely a spot on earth  where its subject can rest easy  there were several candidates for this  top job but the organization elected  already  the uae categorically rejects the  accusations leveled against him  interpol did not respond to the specific  allegations  they sent us this written statement  it is the general assembly interpol  supreme governing body which elects  members of the executive committee it  would therefore be inappropriate for the  general secretariat to comment on any of  the candidates  lawyer rodney dickson represents hedges  and ahmad  he filed a criminal complaint here in  turkey against al-raysi  and we are saying that the right  decision would be to open a case  and arrest him for these crimes and then  where there's sufficient evidence look  to prosecute those crimes under  universal jurisdiction here in istanbul  this is what hedges and ahmad hoped for  the idea that the man in whom they see  their torturer  becomes the world's leading police  officer  is unbearable to them  let's get reaction from an expert in  criminal justice i'm joined by bruno min  he's legal director for the ngo fair  trial bruno man thanks so much for your  time what do you make of this  appointment well i think the first thing  that we have to bear in mind is that the  role of interpol's presidency is largely  a ceremonial largely symbolic role so  the idea is that although this is a high  profile position  they don't have the president doesn't  have  uh an influence over the day-to-day  operations of the organization including  uh decisions regarding um  who  does and doesn't get a red notice which  is an alert used by countries through  interpol systems to  track down fugitives for the purpose of  arrest and extradition  but having said that um appearances do  matter and we have to  take into consideration obviously that  um this the head of the world's police  as far as the rest of the world is  concerned there's someone w